STEPS (for each sheet)
----------------------
  1. Print the page from the print PDF at 100 % ({{ L('pdf_actual_size') }}, no "fit to page"),
     one sheet at a time. The PDF turns itself to portrait: do not change the orientation.
  2. Let the ink dry, ideally overnight (dye ink).
  3. Notch the laminate first, for every finish: cut {{ notch_dxf }} on the laminate sheet
     (plain cut, no registration marks, placed at X 0 / Y 0), so the three
     {{ "%g"|format(sheet.notch) }} × {{ "%g"|format(sheet.notch) }} mm corners are open. Lay the laminate with its
     notches over the three registration marks, then laminate.
  4. Silhouette Studio, page {{ L('landscape') }}: {{ L('file_menu') }} → {{ L('open') }} the template in the
     table above (the .studio3, or one built from the .svg). Check {{ L('reg_marks') }}:
     {{ L('type1') }}, {{ L('length') }} {{ "%g"|format(sheet.mark_length) }} mm, {{ L('thickness') }} {{ "%g"|format(sheet.mark_thickness) }} mm, {{ L('inset') }} {{ "%g"|format(sheet.mark_inset) }} mm.
     Load the sheet on the mat in landscape, like the card proxies: the filled square mark
     at the top left.
  5. {{ L('send') }}: kiss cut through the laminate and the vinyl, not the backing
     with the finish's {{ L('material') }} (a {{ L('test_cut') }} first on each new finish or roll;
     starting settings in docs/cut-settings.md).
  6. Couper la feuille aux traits de coupe en trois tiers (haut / milieu / bas).
     (Trim the sheet at the trim ticks into its three pieces, then pack each piece with the
     packing slip: every piece ships flat in a #10 envelope.)
